## ✨ What is Mood Sync?

**Mood Sync** detects your facial emotion in real time and automatically curates music that matches your mood — all inside a sleek cyberpunk-themed UI. Listen together with friends in synced rooms, chat, draw on a shared whiteboard, and track your emotional journey over time.

---

## 🚀 Features

| Feature | Description |
|---|---|
| 🎭 **Emotion Detection** | Real-time facial emotion recognition via `face-api.js` |
| 🎵 **Mood-Based Music** | Auto-curates tracks from JioSaavn & Spotify based on your emotion |
| 🔊 **Audio Visualizer** | Live frequency bar visualizer using Web Audio API |
| 🏠 **Sync Rooms** | Create or join rooms to listen in perfect sync with friends |
| 💬 **Live Chat** | In-room real-time chat powered by Firebase |
| 🎨 **Whiteboard** | Collaborative drawing canvas shared across room members |
| 👥 **Friends Panel** | See what your friends are currently listening to |
| 📊 **Mood Insights** | Charts and history of your emotional listening patterns |
| 🌗 **Dark / Light Theme** | Toggle between themes with smooth transitions |
| ✨ **Particle Field** | Animated ambient particle background |

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

```
Frontend       →  React 19 + TypeScript + TailwindCSS v4 + Framer Motion
Routing        →  TanStack Router + TanStack Query
UI Components  →  Radix UI + shadcn/ui
Auth           →  Firebase Auth + Supabase Auth
Database       →  Firebase Realtime DB + Supabase (PostgreSQL)
Music APIs     →  Spotify Web API + JioSaavn API
AI / Vision    →  face-api.js (TensorFlow.js)
Build          →  Vite 7 + Bun
Deploy         →  Cloudflare Workers (via Wrangler)
```

---

## ⚡ Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- [Bun](https://bun.sh) or Node.js 18+
- Firebase project with Realtime Database enabled
- Supabase project
- Spotify Developer App (for Spotify integration)

### 1. Clone & Install

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/music-main.git
cd music-main
bun install        # or: npm install
```

### 2. Configure Environment

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in your keys:

```env
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=<your_firebase_api_key>
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=<your_auth_domain>
VITE_FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL=<your_database_url>
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=<your_project_id>
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=<your_supabase_url>
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<your_supabase_anon_key>
VITE_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=<your_spotify_client_id>
```

### 3. Run Locally

```bash
bun run dev        # starts Vite dev server + Express proxy
```

Open [http://localhost:5173](http://localhost:5173) 🎉

